                                                "sense_id": "533aa649-55d1-3198-8165-96d7ce837b28",
                                                "text": "On the November morning when the sulfur burps began, Derron Borders was welcoming prospective students at the graduate school where he works in New York. […] Sulfur burps appear to be a somewhat rare side effect of semaglutide, tirzepatide, and other drugs in their class, known as GLP-1 receptor agonists."
